  [;; The decision plane left this repository on 2026-08-21 (root
   ;; ADR-2608219500). Nineteen entries went with it -- enrolment, update and
   ;; release admission, trusted time, the authority schema, the policy
   ;; reasoner, the capability broker, manifest identity and signing, signer
   ;; lifecycle, the network origin gate, the anchor set, the remote-authority
   ;; decision, the component graph, the provider surface, deployment-profile
   ;; admission, audit emission and boot-artifact admission.
   ;;
   ;; They did not stop being TCB. They became TCB in another repository, and
   ;; the way this inventory says so is the pinned `io.github.kotoba-lang/grant`
   ;; git SHA under :tcb/external. Deleting them without that entry would have
   ;; shrunk the recorded TCB while the real one stayed the same size.
   ;;
   ;; What is left here is the machine: the thing that executes an admitted
   ;; component, and the hardware and boot surfaces it executes it on.

   ;; Account authorization is decided by auth.kotoba.cloud, then bound to the
   ;; exact device DID and one-time challenge here. The hosted adapter owns the
   ;; poll secret and transport; the state machine owns the authenticated and
   ;; claimed transitions. Both can grant device authority and therefore belong
   ;; in this inventory.
